WEBVTT

00:00:00.205 --> 00:00:07.341
The dawn at Mount Rodney.

00:00:10.864 --> 00:00:17.081
Mr. Carson's children allowed Candy to stay
at the barn, without telling their father about it.

00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:25.469
On that night, Susy, the youngest child,
broke out in fever.

00:00:27.205 --> 00:00:30.854
Mr. Carson kept shouting that the doctor
will not come.

00:00:32.068 --> 00:00:39.831
However, Candy took off in belief that the doctor
will come once he learns of the circumstances.

00:01:01.116 --> 00:01:02.065
It's over there!

00:01:11.095 --> 00:01:11.830
Doctor!

00:01:11.986 --> 00:01:14.475
Please!
Doctor!

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.257
Open up, please!

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:19.114
Yes... who is it?

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.874
We have an emergency!
The doctor needs to come right now!

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:25.968
Susy has a big fever!

00:01:26.512 --> 00:01:30.808
Sam... I'll wake him up.
Come inside.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.550
Yes.
Okay?

00:01:38.296 --> 00:01:41.771
What? An emergency?
Who called?

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:46.263
It's mr. Carson's Susy...
She is in a fever...

00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:48.930
What? Carson?

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.228
I can't.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.727
What?

00:01:55.825 --> 00:01:57.753
I can't go to his place.

00:01:58.511 --> 00:02:05.579
But... aren't you supposed to be a doctor?
Isn't helping sick people your job?

00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:11.887
I went there in good will and did an examination. I can't stand
the way they later called me a murderer because of that.

00:02:12.062 --> 00:02:13.603
I'm sorry, but you should go back.

00:02:13.723 --> 00:02:14.566
But...

00:02:15.731 --> 00:02:17.038
Doctor, wait!

00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:19.468
Doctor! Please!

00:02:19.503 --> 00:02:20.859
It won't do any good, sis!

00:02:21.949 --> 00:02:23.076
Sam...

00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:26.161
There's no helping it.
It's my dad's fault.

00:02:29.712 --> 00:02:30.692
Sam!

00:02:32.609 --> 00:02:36.673
Ever since Mom died, he sometimes
gets drunk and wanders around his house.

00:02:37.251 --> 00:02:38.339
It's not because of that!

00:02:38.707 --> 00:02:42.301
No matter what had happened, isn't it doctor's job
to come and to help the sick?

00:02:43.921 --> 00:02:47.699
My dad thinks it's doctor's fault
that mom died!

00:02:52.915 --> 00:02:53.766
Doctor!

00:02:54.188 --> 00:02:55.036
My wife?

00:02:57.027 --> 00:02:58.565
There was nothing I could do...

00:02:58.726 --> 00:03:00.942
What? You couldn't help her?

00:03:05.953 --> 00:03:07.920
You... you murderer!

00:03:11.997 --> 00:03:12.962
Mr. Carson!

00:03:13.105 --> 00:03:14.400
It's not doctor's fault!

00:03:17.138 --> 00:03:18.771
Get out!

00:03:21.256 --> 00:03:23.137
Get the hell out!

00:03:24.926 --> 00:03:31.486
After that, my dad started drinking
and coming to doctor's house.

00:03:35.303 --> 00:03:36.377
Shit!

00:03:37.566 --> 00:03:40.798
You all sided with that doctor...!

00:03:41.702 --> 00:03:44.686
My wife... give her back!

00:03:45.741 --> 00:03:46.740
Give her back!

00:03:50.393 --> 00:03:52.026
Give her back!

00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:58.509
I see. That's why everybody started avoiding him?

00:03:58.927 --> 00:04:00.205
That's right.

00:04:00.637 --> 00:04:03.972
That's exactly why I can't
just leave Susy like this!

00:04:04.961 --> 00:04:06.832
We quickly need to do something...

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.153
Lady!

00:04:13.537 --> 00:04:15.639
How is Susy's condition?

00:04:16.562 --> 00:04:19.764
She suddenly felt exhausted
and broke out in fever...

00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:22.696
The way that fever appeared
seemed out of the ordinary.

00:04:22.743 --> 00:04:25.346
It could be measles.

00:04:25.695 --> 00:04:26.916
Measles?

00:04:28.649 --> 00:04:29.903
If it's measles...

00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:32.063
We should treat her somehow?

00:04:32.589 --> 00:04:33.774
That's right...

00:04:36.656 --> 00:04:39.260
See? I told you the doctor won't come!

00:04:40.653 --> 00:04:44.013
It's okay. I will help her.

00:04:44.263 --> 00:04:45.554
What? You?

00:04:48.285 --> 00:04:50.816
You think I'd let you mess around my daughter?

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.697
Moreover... haven't I told you to get lost?

00:04:56.814 --> 00:04:58.036
The rash is coming out!

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.298
I'm sure it's measles!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.705
Measles?

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.367
I've seen it many times in Pony's home...

00:05:13.608 --> 00:05:15.525
-Mr. Carson!
-What?

00:05:16.419 --> 00:05:19.890
Please hurry and bring some dry clothes
for Susy to change into.

00:05:22.057 --> 00:05:23.778
Are you ordering me?

00:05:23.963 --> 00:05:29.273
Susy's illness is contagious.
Have Sam and Jeff ever contracted measles?

00:05:30.217 --> 00:05:34.043
We both had it while mom was still alive.
Right?

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:38.628
Mom watched all night over us.

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:42.606
I see. And I'll watch over Susy.

00:05:42.768 --> 00:05:45.469
Thank you, Candy-sis!

00:05:46.163 --> 00:05:50.993
-Sam, bring some cold water.
-Ok!

00:05:52.407 --> 00:05:55.284
-Jeff, and you bring the towels.
-Ok!

00:05:57.973 --> 00:06:05.128
Mr. Carson. Hurry and bring Susy's clothes...
After that, place Susy's bed in the warmest room.

00:06:05.649 --> 00:06:06.492
Alright...

00:06:12.689 --> 00:06:15.019
Susy, hang in there!

00:06:28.295 --> 00:06:32.779
Mr. Carson! Please don't make so much noise!
You'll upset her.

00:06:34.679 --> 00:06:37.015
I'm worried sick...

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:41.171
Why don't you take a nap?
I'll watch over her.

00:06:43.609 --> 00:06:46.344
Please do...
I just can't watch her like this.

00:06:50.093 --> 00:06:50.873
Dad.

00:06:51.036 --> 00:06:52.136
How is Susy doing?

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:55.393
Don't worry. Go to bed now.

00:06:55.428 --> 00:06:59.351
-Dad, will she really be okay?
-She'll be okay?

00:07:00.118 --> 00:07:04.456
Yeah, I think so.
She's not gonna die.

00:07:12.628 --> 00:07:15.488
I remember the time Jimmy had a fever.

00:07:16.399 --> 00:07:21.198
I didn't know what to do...
I just panicked.

00:07:28.786 --> 00:07:34.440
Candy, it's alright. Don't worry,
return to your room and go to sleep.

00:07:34.849 --> 00:07:35.642
Okay.

00:07:37.939 --> 00:07:42.359
Sister Pony and sister Lane tirelessly
nursed him back to health.

00:07:48.181 --> 00:07:52.645
Susy, I'm sure you'll be fine. Instead of your mom,
I'll nurse you back to health.

00:07:53.458 --> 00:07:57.496
-Bro, Susy will get better, right?
-Of course!

00:07:57.655 --> 00:08:00.022
Candy-sis is so kind!

00:08:01.241 --> 00:08:02.215
Yeah.

00:08:02.681 --> 00:08:04.699
She is just like a real sister!

00:08:05.937 --> 00:08:06.880
Bro!

00:08:10.631 --> 00:08:11.739
It's dad!

00:08:13.545 --> 00:08:18.221
He's probably praying for Mom to quickly
return from behind Mount Rodney, right?

00:08:18.417 --> 00:08:19.428
Jeff...

00:08:20.255 --> 00:08:23.416
If Mom comes back, he wouldn't be
so confused anymore, right?

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:28.126
This guy... when is he going to realize
that mom died?

00:08:32.459 --> 00:08:35.064
Please... save Susy.

00:08:36.331 --> 00:08:40.037
I'm begging you... give her some strength.

00:08:46.165 --> 00:08:47.561
Mom...

00:08:48.533 --> 00:08:50.115
Mom...

00:08:50.593 --> 00:08:51.854
I'm right here.

00:08:53.275 --> 00:08:55.281
Susy, I'm here.

00:09:15.711 --> 00:09:16.961
Mom...

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.508
Mom.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.416
Susy!

00:09:28.806 --> 00:09:30.278
You're better!

00:09:30.948 --> 00:09:33.013
Candy-mom.

00:09:33.424 --> 00:09:38.222
Susy. Thank goodness, Susy!

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.190
Susy!
What happened?

00:09:48.221 --> 00:09:49.721
Dad!

00:09:50.795 --> 00:09:52.125
Susy!

00:09:52.223 --> 00:09:53.823
She's alright.

00:09:56.883 --> 00:09:58.542
Susy!

00:09:59.452 --> 00:10:00.497
Susy!

00:10:01.263 --> 00:10:03.377
Thank goodness, Susy!

00:10:08.387 --> 00:10:09.663
Thank goodness.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.883
Susy!

00:10:19.928 --> 00:10:20.757
Susy!

00:10:20.934 --> 00:10:23.124
You're already awake?

00:10:23.201 --> 00:10:24.906
We couldn't sleep from worry.

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:26.133
Bro!

00:10:26.317 --> 00:10:27.450
You're better, Susy!

00:10:27.704 --> 00:10:29.313
You're better, Susy!

00:10:33.314 --> 00:10:34.894
That's great, Susy!

00:10:35.213 --> 00:10:36.755
That's great, Susy!

00:10:38.212 --> 00:10:40.572
Thank goodness!
Truly, thank goodness!

00:10:45.098 --> 00:10:47.252
Huh? A carriage is coming this way.

00:10:49.976 --> 00:10:52.562
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
-Translator: The name "Susy" is mentioned 43 times in this episode.
Am I the only one who finds it annoying?
-Timing guy: Tell me about it.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:58.473
It's that doctor!

00:10:58.848 --> 00:11:01.043
He must have been worried about her.

00:11:03.217 --> 00:11:05.607
Now he shows up?!

00:11:11.648 --> 00:11:13.751
You killer! Wha'cha come here for, eh?

00:11:14.427 --> 00:11:16.246
I'm gonna beat the snot out of you!

00:11:17.156 --> 00:11:20.563
-That's why I didn't want to come here anymore...
-Wait!

00:11:21.127 --> 00:11:22.253
Mr. Carson!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:24.165
Stop that, dad!

00:11:24.429 --> 00:11:25.839
Don't do that, dad!

00:11:28.161 --> 00:11:28.810
Wait!

00:11:28.998 --> 00:11:31.379
-Stop, mr. Carson!
-Stop!

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:32.733
-Let go of me!
-Don't do that!

00:11:32.768 --> 00:11:35.649
-Let go!
-You're wrong for hating the doctor!

00:11:37.237 --> 00:11:40.458
Susy got well because of doctor!

00:11:41.724 --> 00:11:44.316
Why do you say it's his doing? Shit!

00:11:44.383 --> 00:11:47.822
Doctor's wife told us how to treat Susy!

00:11:49.376 --> 00:11:53.982
If she hadn't told us what to do,
we might not have been able to help Susy.

00:12:01.059 --> 00:12:07.198
Mr. Carson, no matter how hard the doctor might try,
try to understand that there are incurable diseases.

00:12:07.362 --> 00:12:10.517
Doctor, are you here to see Susy?

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:15.735
That's exactly why I came.
I couldn't sleep from worry.

00:12:16.798 --> 00:12:17.735
This way.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.853
No need to worry anymore.
Thank goodness!

00:12:28.193 --> 00:12:29.947
You did well, Candy.

00:12:30.662 --> 00:12:33.245
You were a great nurse.

00:12:34.978 --> 00:12:37.437
Me? A nurse?

00:12:41.851 --> 00:12:44.869
Sam, stop by at my place
to pick up the medicine.

00:12:45.145 --> 00:12:45.865
Okay!

00:12:46.945 --> 00:12:48.192
Thank you very much!

00:13:00.294 --> 00:13:02.742
Wow, smells great!

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.941
Smells great, right?

00:13:07.049 --> 00:13:08.014
Lemme see...

00:13:08.049 --> 00:13:10.183
Hey, Sam! Those are bad manners!

00:13:11.357 --> 00:13:12.944
Bad manners!

00:13:13.523 --> 00:13:17.860
Doesn't matter how good you are,
you can't match the taste of my cooking!

00:13:17.962 --> 00:13:19.706
You're a wise guy, aren't you?

00:13:20.194 --> 00:13:21.823
Hey, Jeff!

00:13:22.694 --> 00:13:24.468
I'm just tasting it...

00:13:39.689 --> 00:13:40.291
There!

00:13:42.615 --> 00:13:43.579
Well?

00:13:44.239 --> 00:13:45.262
Tasty!

00:13:46.335 --> 00:13:47.484
That's great!

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:58.725
Susy was quickly getting better
because of Candy's care.

00:14:04.746 --> 00:14:06.706
There! Say "Aaah".

00:14:12.494 --> 00:14:13.777
Here, Susy!

00:14:16.402 --> 00:14:22.212
Here's a treat because you were patient
and didn't complain while taking the medicine!

00:14:22.635 --> 00:14:25.152
The rash is almost completely gone!

00:14:25.479 --> 00:14:27.988
Sis, you really can make anything!

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.992
Thank you, Candy-mom.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:38.010
-Susy keeps calling you mom!
-I don't mind!

00:14:38.713 --> 00:14:43.793
But you're still too young to be a mom!
You'd better be my bride!

00:14:43.798 --> 00:14:45.648
Sam, you!

00:14:45.669 --> 00:14:47.144
Bro, you're sly!

00:14:50.165 --> 00:14:51.479
You're blushing!

00:15:07.326 --> 00:15:09.194
I haven't felt this good in a while!

00:15:10.578 --> 00:15:14.063
Sam, Jeff, I'm going to climb that tree.

00:15:16.393 --> 00:15:18.655
Candy-sis, you can climb trees?

00:15:19.653 --> 00:15:21.476
I'm great at it!

00:15:22.296 --> 00:15:25.624
I wanted to climb it once Susy got better!

00:15:26.517 --> 00:15:28.878
Sis, you're a tomboy!

00:15:29.019 --> 00:15:30.376
A tomboy!

00:15:30.988 --> 00:15:34.145
That's right!
Okay? Look at me!

00:15:44.533 --> 00:15:46.654
Sis! Do your best!

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.195
Kurin is good, too!

00:15:54.815 --> 00:15:56.622
Do your best, Kurin!

00:16:03.478 --> 00:16:04.833
I can see the sea.

00:16:05.932 --> 00:16:09.428
Kurin, the sea!
I can see the sea!

00:16:17.145 --> 00:16:19.064
America lies across that sea.

00:16:23.939 --> 00:16:25.644
America, where Terry is right now.

00:16:27.685 --> 00:16:30.660
...and my dearest Pony's home.

00:16:37.301 --> 00:16:41.524
It's going to start snowing soon.
I'd better board a ship before then.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:08.174
Here!

00:17:08.334 --> 00:17:09.046
Here.

00:17:10.004 --> 00:17:10.648
Here!

00:17:11.306 --> 00:17:12.098
Here.

00:17:18.786 --> 00:17:22.208
-Uh... miss Candy...
-Yes?

00:17:22.473 --> 00:17:25.444
-Could you come over for a minute?
-Okay.

00:17:30.156 --> 00:17:36.448
I owe you so much for taking care of Susy.
This is too little but...

00:17:36.625 --> 00:17:42.035
It's okay! I don't need money.
I did this because I like children.

00:17:46.078 --> 00:17:47.316
Actually...

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:48.972
I want you to leave.

00:17:53.153 --> 00:17:55.893
You're just at a stopover at our house.

00:17:56.125 --> 00:17:59.996
Please, leave before children
start liking you even more.

00:18:02.018 --> 00:18:07.776
If you leave before everybody wakes up,
maybe your departure won't be so hard on them?

00:18:08.793 --> 00:18:10.712
It's exactly like you said.

00:18:11.163 --> 00:18:13.618
I will leave tomorrow at dawn.

00:18:16.272 --> 00:18:21.903
Please take it, even if it's so little.
It's the best I could do.

00:18:22.273 --> 00:18:25.635
Really, I'm fine. I'll get along somehow.

00:18:34.704 --> 00:18:42.094
Susy, you'll be just fine.
I'm so glad you got well.

00:18:45.651 --> 00:18:46.675
Jeff.

00:18:49.814 --> 00:18:52.131
Listen to your brother!

00:18:55.338 --> 00:18:56.310
Sam.

00:18:56.715 --> 00:19:01.024
With you around, I know that
Susy and Jeff will be safe.

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:03.590
Stay well!

00:19:10.265 --> 00:19:13.926
Farewell... everyone.
Stay well!

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:16.420
Sis!

00:19:20.406 --> 00:19:21.515
Sam...

00:19:23.893 --> 00:19:26.033
I heard you talking.

00:19:27.613 --> 00:19:31.882
I... I don't want to hold back.

00:19:32.417 --> 00:19:33.536
Sam...

00:19:34.349 --> 00:19:40.998
Susy and Jeff will be okay!
Therefore... sis, take care!

00:19:49.099 --> 00:19:50.264
Sam.

00:20:03.947 --> 00:20:05.570
Farewell!

00:20:09.314 --> 00:20:14.769
Susy, Jeff, Sam.
Everyone... stay well!

00:20:15.433 --> 00:20:17.766
Farewell, mr. Carson!

00:20:19.641 --> 00:20:22.256
I wrote you a letter of introduction.

00:20:23.344 --> 00:20:29.045
A friend of mine, Juskin, is running
a shipping company in Southampton's port.

00:20:30.297 --> 00:20:31.705
Mr. Carson!

00:20:31.885 --> 00:20:36.788
His company has probably grown quite a bit.
You can look for him.

00:20:37.875 --> 00:20:40.927
He saved me from what I dreaded the most.
Thank you, mr. Carson!

00:20:41.087 --> 00:20:43.870
Farewell, Candy-sis!

00:20:47.898 --> 00:20:49.914
Farewell!

00:20:56.545 --> 00:21:00.029
Sadness always follows parting people.

00:21:00.943 --> 00:21:04.453
However, this sadness doesn't last forever.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:11.545
Candy cheered up, heading
towards the port of Southampton.

00:21:13.532 --> 00:21:20.287
To be continued...
